    airo:evidenceText "ElevenLabs’ website says the company was founded by Piotr Dabkowski, an ex-Google machine learning engineer, and Mati Staniszewski, an ex-Palantir deployment strategist." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e8a00aa5495> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This month the company announced a $2 million pre-seed round led by Czech venture capital firm Credo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7616d9045f8a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Startup Shocked When 4Chan Immediately Abuses Its Voice-Cloning AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8027" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/83ef48fd5ba7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Many social media companies, including Meta and Twitch, have banned deepfakes and manipulated videos that deceive users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2618" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c72fb433679> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Es una empresa checa creada por Piotr Dabkowski —un ingeniero de aprendizaje automático que laboró en Google—." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d8e68783cc33> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meta, which owns Facebook and Instagram, ran a competition in 2021 to develop programs capable of identifying deepfakes, resulting in one tool that could spot them 83 percent of the time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2618" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eacae4586676> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Graphika, a research firm that studies disinformation, spotted deepfakes of fictional news anchors that pro-China bot accounts distributed late last year, in the first known example of the technology’s being used for state-aligned influence campaigns." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2618" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f185b0971e98> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Es una empresa checa creada por ... y Mati Staniszewski —un estratega de implementación —." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/20fb7647da9c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company, founded in 2022 by former Google machine learning engineer Piotr Dabkowski and ex-Palantir deployment strategist Mati Staniszewski, addressed the issue on Twitter after Vice found clips on 4chan featuring what sound like auto-generated celebrity voices making questionable statements." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8028" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/72d9e9a354dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "4chan members used ElevenLabs to make deepfake voices of Emma Watson, Joe Rogan, and others saying racist, transphobic, and violent things." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c50389b8478c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ElevenLabs offers \"speech synthesis\" and \"voice cloning\"—the latter of which results in a clean sample recording, more than one minute in length." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8028" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe2de1d676ac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft recently announced an artificial intelligence program called VALL-E that can clone someone's voice from a three-second audio clip." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2668" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c07be2da8ff9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The chatbot ChatGPT and the image generators Stable Diffusion, DALL-E and Midjourney are all promising to revolutionise and disrupt the creative industries and other businesses." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2668" .

